        "The work breakdown structure (WBS) divides a project into deliverables and work packages small enough to estimate and assign, typically two weeks of effort or less. Milestones are zero-duration checkpoints marking completion of major deliverables: requirements signed, database migrated, system live. The WBS is the backbone that schedules and budgets hang on. In {S}, a missing WBS shows immediately: tasks like do the website cannot be tracked, assigned or paid for.",
