        "The critical path is the longest chain of dependent tasks: it fixes the shortest possible project duration, and any delay on it delays delivery. Tasks off the critical path have float, slack time they can slip without moving the end date. For a chain of 3, 5 and 2 days against a parallel 4 and 4, the critical path totals 10 days and the parallel path carries 2 days of float. In {S}, rushing non-critical tasks buys nothing; attack the chain that governs the date.",
