        "Documentation is the project's memory. The proposal records intent and cost; the requirements document records what was agreed; design documents record how; the user manual explains operation in the user's language; technical documentation lets a successor maintain the system. Writing happens alongside building, not after. In {S}, the examinable distinction is audience: a manual for users, a maintenance guide for engineers, and never one document pretending to be both.",
