        "Trace an IoT parking sensor. A magnetometer at each space detects a car (sense), sends the reading over a low-power radio to a gateway (connect), the backend marks the space and a display shows availability (decide and act), and parking officers receive a queue ordered by expiry time. The data also builds occupancy history for pricing. In {S}, this single example carries the section's vocabulary: sensor, gateway, actuator, analytics, all in one story.",
        "Classify cloud services by example. A startup rents virtual machines and object storage: IaaS. The same startup deploys its code on a managed platform that scales itself: PaaS. A school pays per user per month for email, documents and video meetings: SaaS. The exam question inverted, given Gmail, AWS EC2 or Heroku, name the model, is the form {S} papers prefer, and the answer rule is: how much does the provider manage?",
        "See how a model learns. To predict palm-oil prices, a team gathers five years of daily prices, exchange rates and rainfall; splits the data into training and test sets; trains a regression model; then scores it on the untouched test set, because scoring on training data flatters the model. Deployment adds monitoring, since markets drift. In {S}, the train-test split and the monitoring step are the two details that separate serious work from a screenshot.",
