        "Security practice must scale with adoption. Smart meters exposed by default passwords become a grid problem, not a gadget problem; a biased scoring model denies loans to whole postcodes; a leaked biometric database cannot be reissued like a card. The Nigeria Data Protection Act gives rights and duties, and NITDA issues guidelines for public-sector systems. In {S}, governance questions now appear in the same paper as technical ones, and both carry marks.",
