        "A sample project outline. Problem: students miss departmental announcements. Users: students and the course adviser. Screens: announcements list, single announcement, admin post form, login. Data: announcements (id, title, body, date, author) and users (id, name, role). Feature: admin posting with confirmation. In {S}, this is four screens and two tables, finishable in three weeks, and every later decision, testing included, refers back to this page.",
        "A worked storage check for the capstone. Suppose the site ships with 40 images of 300 KB and a database of 20 MB. Assets are 40 x 300 KB = 12,000 KB, which is 12 MB, plus 20 MB of data, so about 32 MB, and a 100 MB hosting plan leaves ample headroom for growth and backups. In {S}, this two-line calculation, assets plus data against plan size, is the planning check most skipped and most regretted.",
        "A drill routine that works. Take a past paper of 60 objectives in 60 minutes; mark strictly; sort the misses into definition, application or calculation; drill the weakest bucket with fresh questions the next day, and retest after three days. Most candidates gain more marks moving a weak section from D to B than pushing an A section higher. In {S}, that triage, sort, drill, retest, is the whole method.",
